- ✔ reconciliation MATCHED

**9. Explanation**

The reversal is an operation like any other, with the same lookup-before-submit rule. Fineract's undo keeps the repayment, marks it reversed and stores our reference on it (`reversalExternalId`), so a lost answer is resolved by looking the repayment up, never by undoing it twice.

The reversing journal entry is the repayment's own entry with debits and credits swapped, posted as `{repayment}:REVERSAL`. The ERP is unique on that reference, so there is one reversing entry per repayment whatever the reversal is called.

